      "problem": "Let $c=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $d=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $d$ onto $c.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{c}\\,d & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{c\\cdot c}c \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{c}_{x}^{2}+{c}_{y}^{2}+{c}_{z}^{2}}c \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 3+5\\cdot (-2)+0\\cdot 4}{{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+{0}^{2}}c \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{26}⟨1,5,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{7}{26},-\\frac{35}{26},0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
